#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:314
msgid "Importing `__attribute__((NSObject))` variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:316
msgid ""
"GCC introduces `__attribute__((NSObject))` on structure pointers to mean "
"\"this is an object\". This is useful because many low level data structures "
"are declared as opaque structure pointers, e.g. `CFStringRef`, `CFArrayRef`, "
"etc. When used from C, however, these are still really objects and are the "
"second case where that requires copy and dispose helper functions to be "
"generated. The copy helper functions generated by the compiler should use "
"the `_Block_object_assign` runtime helper function and in the dispose helper "
"the `_Block_object_dispose` runtime helper function should be called."
msgstr ""

