msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:540
msgid ""
"A `__block` variable that is also marked `__attribute__((NSObject))` should "
"have `byref_keep` and `byref_dispose` helper functions that use "
"`_Block_object_assign` and `_Block_object_dispose`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:544
msgid "`__block` escapes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:546
msgid ""
"Because `Blocks` referencing `__block` variables may have `Block_copy()` "
"performed upon them the underlying storage for the variables may move to the "
"heap. In Objective-C Garbage Collection Only compilation environments the "
"heap used is the garbage collected one and no further action is required. "
"Otherwise the compiler must issue a call to potentially release any heap "
"storage for `__block` variables at all escapes or terminations of their "
"scope. The call should be:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:558
msgid "Nesting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:560
msgid ""
"`Blocks` may contain `Block` literal expressions. Any variables used within "
"inner blocks are imported into all enclosing `Block` scopes even if the "
"variables are not used. This includes `const` imports as well as `__block` "
"variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:565
msgid "Objective C Extensions to `Blocks`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:567
msgid "Importing Objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:569
msgid ""
"Objects should be treated as `__attribute__((NSObject))` variables; all "
"`copy_helper`, `dispose_helper`, `byref_keep`, and `byref_dispose` helper "
"functions should use `_Block_object_assign` and `_Block_object_dispose`. "
"There should be no code generated that uses `*-retain` or `*-release` "
"methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:575
msgid "`Blocks` as Objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:577
msgid ""
"The compiler will treat `Blocks` as objects when synthesizing property "
"setters and getters, will characterize them as objects when generating "
"garbage collection strong and weak layout information in the same manner as "
"objects, and will issue strong and weak write-barrier assignments in the "
"same manner as objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:583
msgid "`__weak __block` Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:585
msgid ""
"Objective-C (and Objective-C++) support the `__weak` attribute on `__block` "
"variables. Under normal circumstances the compiler uses the Objective-C "
"runtime helper support functions `objc_assign_weak` and `objc_read_weak`. "
"Both should continue to be used for all reads and writes of `__weak __block` "
"variables:"
