#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:707
msgid "C++ Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:709
msgid ""
"Within a block stack based C++ objects are copied into `const` copies using "
"the copy constructor. It is an error if a stack based C++ object is used "
"within a block if it does not have a copy constructor. In addition both copy "
"and destroy helper routines must be synthesized for the block to support the "
"`Block_copy()` operation, and the flags work marked with the (1\\<<26) bit "
"in addition to the (1\\<<25) bit. The copy helper should call the "
"constructor using appropriate offsets of the variable within the supplied "
"stack based block source and heap based destination for all `const` "
"constructed copies, and similarly should call the destructor in the destroy "
"routine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Block-ABI-Apple.md:719
msgid ""
"As an example, suppose a C++ class `FOO` existed with a copy constructor. "
"Within a code block a stack version of a `FOO` object is declared and used "
"within a `Block` literal expression:"
